# Provenance of the RTL this repository copies from the AmigaCD core.
#
# NONE OF THE FILES BELOW ARE CANONICAL HERE. They are built in the core, which
# is the only place they are synthesised; they exist here because their
# testbenches do (rtl/tb/*_tb.v) and Icarus needs the sources beside them. Fix a
# bug in the core and re-vendor. Fixing it in a copy means the two diverge and
# the next sync quietly reverts you.
#
# rtl/snac_psx.v is NOT in this list and is the one exception: it is canonical
# HERE, and both core repos take a copy of it. See rtl/README.md, which sets out
# which way round each file goes and why.
#
# This is checked in CI: ./core_rtl_vendor_check.sh. If that step fails, do NOT
# restamp to make it green -- restamping records whatever is here as correct,
# which is the one thing the check exists to doubt.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. It already went wrong, silently, for two commits. On 2026-09-15
# rtl/ss_ctrl.v here was behind the core's: the core had registered its DDR3
# read return (a timing fix, eleven of the design's worst twelve paths) and
# dropped the rom_scan term from the SDRAM port mux, and neither had been copied
# over. Both repositories' CI was green the whole time. rtl/tb/ss_ctrl_tb.v --
# which the core's own source comments cite as the proof of that wiring -- was
# running against a module the core had stopped building.
#
# repo_former is the core's name before its 2026-09-15 GitHub rename. The rename
# is a settings action that had not happened when this stamp was written, so the
# check accepts either name; delete that line once every clone has been
# re-pointed.
#
# Refresh with: ./core_rtl_vendor_check.sh --stamp /path/to/core-checkout

repo   = FringeCoder/AmigaCD_MiSTer
repo_former = FringeCoder/Minimig-AGA-cd32-cdtv-native-akiko
vendored = 2026-10-02

